# Database & Storage
# Floor is 1.19.1, where autogenerate began comparing CHECK constraints. The
# cap that used to sit here is gone: alembic/env.py's `include_object` now
# extends the one-directional drift contract to `check_constraint`, so the
# raw-SQL CHECKs with no ORM counterpart are exempt the same way raw-SQL
# tables and indexes already were. Three ORM constraints that the DDL had
# created under different names were renamed to match rather than exempted.
# Proven against a live migrated schema, not assumed: the gate fails at 1.19.1
# without the fix (29 operations), passes with it, and still fails when an
# ORM-only CHECK is introduced — so the blind spot did not widen.
